% ============================================================================
% ADJ52 case-21 derived rulebook.
% Clinical area: bladder mass presenting with paroxysmal catecholamine-type
% autonomic spells (urology / endocrinology cross-over).
%
% The diagnostic puzzle the IR poses (q1-q5): a vascular, avidly/uniformly
% enhancing bladder DOME mass plus 3 years of recurrent, stereotyped autonomic
% spells (pounding heartbeat, profuse sweating, throbbing frontal headache,
% nausea/vomiting, feeling drained/shaky) that come on SHORTLY AFTER VOIDING,
% culminating in an abrupt intraoperative hypertensive crisis (175/105) right
% after induction/manipulation. That conjunction is the textbook picture of a
% CATECHOLAMINE-SECRETING URINARY BLADDER PARAGANGLIOMA (extra-adrenal
% pheochromocytoma of the bladder): micturition mechanically squeezes the tumor,
% releasing a bolus of catecholamines -> the post-void spell; surgical
% manipulation does the same -> the intraoperative crisis.
%
% Magnitudes are encoded QUALITATIVELY per adj-lang grammar (lowercase, no
% leading digit, no uppercase). E.g. contrast_enhancement(avid_uniform),
% spell_trigger(post_voiding), intraop_event(hypertensive_crisis_on_manipulation).
%
% Anti-overfit note: every clause is added because a cited source supports the
% DIRECTION of the likelihood ratio for that finding in that disease, NOT to make
% this case land on a chosen answer. The tempting wrong answer for a "bladder
% mass" is urothelial carcinoma; discriminators that argue AGAINST it (LR<1) are
% included only where a source supports the direction (e.g. painless hematuria is
% the urothelial-Ca hallmark and is explicitly DENIED here; intense uniform
% hypervascular enhancement and a catecholamine spell pattern favor paraganglioma
% over urothelial Ca per the cited differentiation studies).
% ============================================================================

% ===== PRIORS (base rates for a bladder mass workup in a patient with spells) =====

% rationale: among ALL bladder tumors a paraganglioma is vanishingly rare (~0.05%),
% but conditioned on a bladder mass PLUS paroxysmal catecholamine-type spells the
% pretest probability is materially higher; we set a modest prior and let the engine
% EARN the conclusion from the spell/enhancement/intraop discriminators.
prior 0.18 for diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "Frontiers Surg 2025 10.3389/fsurg.2025.1657833 (bladder PGL ~0.05% of bladder tumors); PMC4518387 (catecholamine PGL)" trust authoritative

% rationale: urothelial carcinoma is by far the commonest bladder mass and is the
% default working diagnosis when a polypoid enhancing bladder lesion is found, so it
% carries the highest prior and must be argued DOWN by the catecholamine features.
prior 0.45 for diagnosis(urothelial_carcinoma)
  source "AAFP 2017 Bladder Cancer Dx/Tx; Medscape 438262 (urothelial Ca commonest bladder tumor, painless hematuria)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a primary panic / anxiety disorder was the prior working label and
% genuinely mimics catecholamine spells; modest prior, to be argued down by the
% structural mass and the micturition/manipulation triggers.
prior 0.12 for diagnosis(panic_anxiety_disorder)
  source "PMC2693284 (pheochromocytoma mimics panic disorder; sympathetic activation reproduces same signs)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a benign or inflammatory bladder lesion (e.g. polyp, cystitis-related
% nodule) is a residual structural possibility for an incidental wall lesion.
prior 0.10 for diagnosis(benign_bladder_lesion)
  source "AAFP 2017 Bladder Cancer Dx/Tx (benign/inflammatory bladder lesions in the differential of a wall nodule)" trust authoritative

% ===== CORRELATED CATECHOLAMINE-EXCESS SPELL (ONE syndrome -> fires ONCE) =====
% rationale: the pounding heartbeat, profuse sweating, throbbing frontal headache,
% lightheadedness, nausea/vomiting and the drained/shaky feeling are NOT independent
% facts — they are the single correlated catecholamine-surge paroxysm described as a
% syndrome in every source. Counting a separate LR for each would double-count one
% mechanism and saturate the posterior, so they are grouped under ONE mechanism
% directive that fires a single combined LR if ANY manifestation is observed.
% mechanism catecholamine_surge for diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma) lr 8.0 : symptom(palpitations), symptom(profuse_sweating), symptom(throbbing_frontal_headache), symptom(lightheadedness), symptom(nausea), symptom_occasional(vomiting), symptom(drained_and_shaky)
% rationale: the same paroxysmal autonomic cluster is exactly what a panic attack
% reproduces, so the syndrome RAISES panic too (this is why it was misdiagnosed) —
% fires once, modestly, for the anxiety conclusion.
% mechanism catecholamine_surge for diagnosis(panic_anxiety_disorder) lr 2.0 : symptom(palpitations), symptom(profuse_sweating), symptom(throbbing_frontal_headache), symptom(lightheadedness), symptom(nausea), symptom_occasional(vomiting), symptom(drained_and_shaky)

% ===== BLADDER PARAGANGLIOMA (catecholamine-secreting) =====

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR — the temporal link of the spells to MICTURITION
% (attacks build in the minutes after voiding) is the near-pathognomonic clue:
% bladder emptying mechanically compresses the tumor and triggers catecholamine
% release. This is the single most specific feature pointing at bladder PGL.
contributes 9.0 from spell_trigger(post_voiding) to diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "Frontiers Oncol 2025 10.3389/fonc.2025.1624336; PMC4444169 (micturition-induced spells; temporal link vital clue)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR — an abrupt hypertensive crisis right after
% induction / on manipulation of the mass is the catecholamine-release signature of
% a functional PGL and is the classic intraoperative hazard reported for these
% tumors. Strongly specific.
contributes 8.0 from intraop_event(hypertensive_crisis_on_manipulation) to diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "PMC3797305 (unsuspected bladder PGL with intraoperative hypertensive crises); PMC3016130 (BP on bladder manipulation)" trust authoritative

% rationale: intense, UNIFORM, avid contrast enhancement of the mass reflects the
% hypervascular chromaffin tumor and favors PGL over urothelial Ca (whose enhancement
% is typically less avid and more heterogeneous).
contributes 3.0 from contrast_enhancement(avid_uniform) to diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "PubMed 34973050 (bladder PGL: uniform marked enhancement, hypervascular); PMC6874976 (PGL vs urothelial Ca enhancement)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a mass arising from the DOME (or antero-superior wall) is the
% characteristic location for bladder PGL (dome/trigone predilection).
contributes 2.0 from mass_location(bladder_dome) to diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "PMC8523196 (bladder PGL most commonly at dome or trigone)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a stereotyped, recurrent paroxysmal pattern over years (rather than a
% steadily progressive complaint) fits an intermittently secreting functional tumor.
contributes 1.6 from spell_pattern(recurrent_stereotyped) to diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "Frontiers Oncol 2025 10.3389/fonc.2025.1624336 (decade-long paroxysmal pattern of functional bladder PGL)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY SYNERGY — a post-voiding spell TOGETHER with an intraoperative
% manipulation crisis is near-specific for a mechanically-squeezable catecholamine
% tumor in the bladder wall; the two triggers share one mechanism (mechanical
% catecholamine release) and their co-occurrence is more than the sum of parts.
interacts 3.0 when spell_trigger(post_voiding) and intraop_event(hypertensive_crisis_on_manipulation) for diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "PMC3016130 (hypertension after micturition AND on manipulation = bladder pheochromocytoma)" trust authoritative

% ===== UROTHELIAL CARCINOMA (the tempting wrong answer — argued DOWN) =====

% rationale: a polypoid enhancing bladder-wall mass is the generic appearance that
% first suggests urothelial Ca, so the structural finding itself supports it.
contributes 2.0 from finding(polypoid_mass) to diagnosis(urothelial_carcinoma)
  source "Medscape 438262 (papillary/polypoid bladder mass typical of urothelial carcinoma)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — painless hematuria is the hallmark of
% urothelial Ca; this patient explicitly DENIES hematuria, which argues against it.
contributes 0.4 from denies(hematuria) to diagnosis(urothelial_carcinoma)
  source "AAFP 2017 Bladder Cancer; Medscape 438262 (painless hematuria is the cardinal urothelial-Ca symptom)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — catecholamine spells precipitated by
% micturition are NOT a feature of urothelial carcinoma; their presence points away
% from a urothelial tumor and toward a functional paraganglioma.
contributes 0.3 from spell_trigger(post_voiding) to diagnosis(urothelial_carcinoma)
  source "PMC6874976 (catecholamine symptom pattern distinguishes bladder PGL from urothelial Ca)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — an abrupt catecholamine-driven crisis
% on bladder manipulation is not expected from a urothelial tumor; it argues against.
contributes 0.4 from intraop_event(hypertensive_crisis_on_manipulation) to diagnosis(urothelial_carcinoma)
  source "PMC3797305 (intraoperative hypertensive crisis is the catecholamine signature of PGL, not urothelial Ca)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE, weak) — intense UNIFORM avid enhancement
% favors a hypervascular PGL over urothelial Ca, whose enhancement is usually less
% avid and more heterogeneous.
contributes 0.6 from contrast_enhancement(avid_uniform) to diagnosis(urothelial_carcinoma)
  source "PMC6874976 (urothelial-Ca enhancement less avid/more heterogeneous than bladder PGL)" trust authoritative

% ===== PANIC / ANXIETY DISORDER (the prior label — argued DOWN) =====

% rationale: the spells were initially attributed to panic/anxiety and partial prior
% response to that framing supports a modest contribution; the syndrome itself is in
% the mechanism above.
contributes 1.3 from prior_diagnosis(presumed_panic_anxiety_disorder) to diagnosis(panic_anxiety_disorder)
  source "PMC2693284 (paroxysmal sympathetic spells routinely first labeled panic/anxiety)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — a structural, avidly-enhancing bladder
% mass is an organic secondary cause that argues strongly against a primary anxiety
% disorder being the whole explanation.
contributes 0.2 from finding(polypoid_mass) to diagnosis(panic_anxiety_disorder)
  source "PMC2693284 (an organic catecholamine source must be excluded before attributing spells to panic)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — spells reproducibly TRIGGERED BY
% MICTURITION are a mechanical/organic signature, not the situational/cognitive
% trigger profile of panic disorder.
contributes 0.3 from spell_trigger(post_voiding) to diagnosis(panic_anxiety_disorder)
  source "Frontiers Oncol 2025 10.3389/fonc.2025.1624336 (micturition-locked spells indicate an organic bladder source, not panic)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — an objectively documented
% intraoperative hypertensive crisis on manipulation is an organic catecholamine
% event incompatible with anxiety as the sole cause.
contributes 0.2 from intraop_event(hypertensive_crisis_on_manipulation) to diagnosis(panic_anxiety_disorder)
  source "PMC2693284 (objective catecholamine crisis points to organic pheochromocytoma/PGL, not panic)" trust authoritative

% ===== BENIGN BLADDER LESION =====

% rationale: a small wall lesion with only scant peripheral blood flow could be a
% benign polyp; weak support from the indolent imaging descriptor.
contributes 1.4 from finding(scant_peripheral_blood_flow) to diagnosis(benign_bladder_lesion)
  source "AAFP 2017 Bladder Cancer Dx/Tx (low-vascularity wall nodule may be benign/inflammatory)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — a catecholamine-driven intraoperative
% crisis is not a feature of a benign inert lesion.
contributes 0.3 from intraop_event(hypertensive_crisis_on_manipulation) to diagnosis(benign_bladder_lesion)
  source "PMC3797305 (a functional catecholamine crisis indicates a secretory tumor, not a benign lesion)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — micturition-triggered autonomic spells
% are not produced by a benign inert lesion.
contributes 0.4 from spell_trigger(post_voiding) to diagnosis(benign_bladder_lesion)
  source "PMC4444169 (micturition-induced catecholamine spells indicate a functional tumor)" trust authoritative

% ===== NEXT STEP (biochemical confirmation BEFORE definitive resection) =====
% rationale: the decisive next step is BIOCHEMICAL confirmation of catecholamine
% excess (plasma free / 24h urinary fractionated metanephrines) BEFORE any further
% resection, so that alpha-blockade can be started pre-op to prevent a hypertensive
% crisis. This is what the neurologist's "rule out secondary causes" should have
% triggered, and it is the standard of care for a suspected functional PGL.
prior 0.22 for next_step(plasma_free_metanephrines_then_alpha_blockade)
  source "Mayo PMET; CAP Testing module; PMC6874976 (plasma free metanephrines = best test; alpha-blockade pre-op)" trust authoritative
contributes 9.0 from spell_trigger(post_voiding) to next_step(plasma_free_metanephrines_then_alpha_blockade)
  source "Frontiers Oncol 2025 10.3389/fonc.2025.1624336 (micturition-locked spells -> measure post-void plasma metanephrines)" trust authoritative
contributes 7.0 from intraop_event(hypertensive_crisis_on_manipulation) to next_step(plasma_free_metanephrines_then_alpha_blockade)
  source "PMC3797305 (intraoperative crisis mandates biochemical PGL workup and pre-op alpha-blockade)" trust authoritative
contributes 3.0 from contrast_enhancement(avid_uniform) to next_step(plasma_free_metanephrines_then_alpha_blockade)
  source "PubMed 34973050 (hypervascular avidly enhancing bladder mass -> exclude functional PGL biochemically)" trust authoritative

% ===== UNCERTAINTIES (decision-relevant, unresolved) =====

% u-metanephrines: catecholamine biochemistry has NOT been measured; elevated
% plasma/urinary fractionated metanephrines would near-confirm a functional PGL, a
% normal result would strongly argue against it. Highest-value discriminator.
contributes 30.0 from metanephrines(elevated) to diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "Mayo PMET (plasma free metanephrines sensitivity ~100% for PGL); CAP Testing module" trust authoritative
contributes 0.1 from metanephrines(normal) to diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "Testing.com plasma free metanephrines (normal metanephrines make PGL extremely unlikely)" trust authoritative
uncertain { metanephrines(elevated), metanephrines(normal) } for diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "Mayo PMET; CAP Testing module (fractionated metanephrines not yet measured; decisive confirmatory test)"

% u-histology: resection histopathology / immunostains (chromogranin, synaptophysin,
% S100 sustentacular) have not yet been reported; PGL histology confirms and
% separates from urothelial Ca (which the lesion can mimic).
contributes 25.0 from histology(chromaffin_paraganglioma) to diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "PMC6874976 (chromogranin/synaptophysin-positive, S100 sustentacular cells confirm bladder PGL)" trust authoritative
contributes 0.1 from histology(urothelial_carcinoma) to diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "PMC6874976 (urothelial-carcinoma histology excludes paraganglioma)" trust authoritative
uncertain { histology(chromaffin_paraganglioma), histology(urothelial_carcinoma) } for diagnosis(bladder_paraganglioma)
  source "PMC6874976 (definitive immunohistochemistry not yet reported; resection histology is confirmatory)"
